Explanation: CKV_AWS_24 flags the SSH (port 22) ingress rule on `aws_security_group.data` because it allowed `0.0.0.0/0` — unrestricted SSH access from the entire internet. The fix scopes that rule's `cidr_blocks` down to a known, trusted range (here reusing the same `203.0.113.0/24` corporate network already used for the MySQL rule) instead of the open internet. If admin access needs to come from more than one location, list each specific CIDR explicitly, or better, remove the direct SSH ingress entirely and require access through a bastion host, AWS Systems Manager Session Manager, or a VPN, so port 22 isn't exposed on this security group at all. The `web` security group's HTTPS-only rule was left untouched, since it's unrelated to this finding and was flagged as intentionally public.
